Human Learning Campaign Three

Title: * 01
You should not expect to survive very long should you choose to ignore the benefits of science.
~
Title: * 01
Research brings not only new types of Soldiers and Weapons but also better Combat skills and advanced Production and Farming methods.
~
Title: * 01
To begin your scientific studies you must first build a Tower of Science.
~
Title: * 01
As with other buildings that hire workers, now build a Tower of Science within the linking distance of your town.
~
Title: * 02
To learn how to Research, Click on your Tower of Science.
~
Button : RESEARCH
Title: * 03
To choose the path of your Research, Click on the Research Icon
~
Title: * 04
Then Click on a category.  Inside the categories you will have a further choice of subjects.
~
Title: * 04
There are usually several levels of research that you can do for each subject.  
~
Title: * 04
Once you have completed one level, your scientists will automatically start on the next.
~
Title: * 04
You may change your Research project at any time.  Any Research completed will not be lost and may be resumed later.
~
Title: * 05
For every nationality there is a Special Unit who possesses advanced skills.  
~
Title: * 05
But you will be unable to train these Special Units until you have researched them.
~
Title: * 05
You will only be able to Research Special Units of a certain nationality if you have a Town of that nationality.
~
Title: * 05
For every Special Unit you may research Berserker skills.  
~
Title: * 05
This enables your Special Units to strike with increased power.  
~
Title: * 05
Berserker research will proceed automatically upon completion of the Special Unit research.
~
Title: * 06
When research on a Special Unit is complete civilians and soldiers will be able to build the Special Structures in which Special Units train.
~
Title: * 06
Special Structures must be built linked to a Town.
~
Title: * 06
Build one of these Special Structures now. 
~
Title: * 06
They will have different names, depending upon nationality.  When a Civilian is building it you will find the button just above the Seat of Power.  
~
Title: * 06
For instance, for Chinese, it is called 'Shao Lin Temple'. Now build one to proceed. 
~
Title: * 07
To learn how to train Special Units, Click on your Special Structure.
~
Button : TRAIN
Title: * 08
Train Special Units in Special Structures the same way that you train Soldiers in Forts.
~ 
Title: * 09
Special Structures, unlike Forts, can only hold eight soldiers.
~ 
Title: * 09
Once trained, the Special Units will remain inside.  
~ 
Title: * 09
You can take them out in exactly the same way that you do with Soldiers in a Fort.  
~ 
Title: * 09
Either Right-Click on them one at a time or take them all out at once with the Sortie Icon.
~ 
Title: * 09
After exiting the Special Structure they should be sent into a Fort to serve under a commander.
~
Title: * 10
You may set Rally Points for Special Structures.  
~
Title: * 10
A Rally Point is the destination at which your men will gather when they have completed their training.
~
Title: * 10
To do this, select the Special Structure and then Right-Click on either a Fort, a Camp or on the ground.  
~
Title: * 10
When you do, a downward pointing finger will mark that position. 
~
Title: * 10
You may change the Rally Point by Right-Clicking on another destination.  
~
Title: * 10
Cancel a Rally-Point by Clicking on the No Rally Point Icon.
~
Title: * 11
If you wish to use War Machines against your enemies rather than Soldiers, you will need to research them in your Towers of Science. 
~
Title: * 11
There are three levels of research that you can do for each type of War Machine.  
~
Title: * 11
The higher the level, the more dangerous the Weapon.
~
Title: * 11
To produce the War Machines you will need to build a War Factory.  
~
Title: * 11
Build one now, making sure that it is linked to a Town. 
~
Title: * 12
To learn how to use War Factory, Click on your War Factory.
~
Button : MAKEWEAP
Title: * 13
With your War Factory selected, Click on the Build Weapons Icon first.
~
Title: * 14
Then Click on the number button above the weapon that you wish to build.  
~
Title: * 14
Only those weapons that you have researched will be visible. For the purpose of the tutorial, all weapons have been made available in this game. 
~
Title: * 14
Continue clicking until the number reaches the number that you wish to build (Max 20).
~
Title: * 14
You may set Rally Points for your weapons as you did for your Special Units.
~
Title: * 15
Seats of Power are very expensive but also very valuable.  
~
Title: * 15
They bring special benefits to your civilization and allow you the opportunity of invoking powerful Greater Beings. 
~
Title: * 15
Every nationality will receive a different benefit from its Seat of Power, so you must take these benefits into account as you plan your strategies.
~
Title: * 15
Build your Seat of Power now, making sure that it is linked to a Town of the same nationality.
~
Title: * 16
To learn how to invoke Greater Beings, Click on your Seat of Power.
~
Button : GB-A1
Title: * 17
From your Seats of Power you may invoke the aid of your Greater Being.
~
Button : GB-A1
Title: * 17
Every Greater Being has unique powers, so plan your strategy with this in mind.
~
Button : GB-A1
Title: * 17
Invoke your Greater Being by selecting your Seat of Power and Clicking on the Invoke Greater Being Icon.  
~
Button : GB-A1
Title: * 17
This Icon will not always be active as you will need a minimum number of Prayer Points for invocation.
~
Title: * 18
To learn how to use Greater Beings, Click on your Greater Being.
~
Title: * 19
Pressing Z on your keyboard will select your Greater Being. Then Click on a target location (like a nearby Independent Town) to attack it. 
~
Title: * 19
Your Greater Being will fly to the target and work its magic.
~
Title: * 19
For some Greater Beings the target will be a large area while for others it can be a building or a single unit.
~
Title: * 20
To learn how to use Special Blessing, Click on your Seat of Power.
~
Button : GB-B1
Title: * 21
When the Power Bar in your seat of power has turned blue, it means that your Prayer Points have reached their maximum.  
~
Button : GB-B1
Title: * 21
You may at this time Click on the Special Blessing Icon.  
~
Title: * 22
When you do you will receive a Special Blessing from your Greater Being.
~
Title: * 22
Although this Special Blessing will use up all of your Prayer Points, it may at times be extraordinarily valuable. 
~
Title: * 23
Press I on your keyboard to select your Inn.
~
Button : HIREUNIT
Title: * 24
Mercenary Soldiers gather at the room at the top of the Inn's interface.  
~
Button : HIREUNIT
Title: * 24
The white number above each shows his leadership level.  
~
Title: * 25
Clicking on a Mercenary will reveal further details including his asking price.
~
Title: * 25
If the price is right, Click on the Hire Mercenary Icon to bring the selected Mercenary into your force.
~
Title: * 25
Mercenaries will come and go from the Inn.  Be patient and wait for one who fits your needs. 
~
Title: * 26
Please select your Inn again.
~
Title: * 27
Skilled Spies may also be hired in your Inns. Spies, both Civilian and Military, will gather in the room on the bottom.  
~
Title: * 28
Hire Spies in the same way that you hire Mercenary Soldiers. Spies are shown on the row below the soldiers. 
~
Title: * 28
Spies hired in Inns are more expensive than those that you train yourself, but if you require skilled Spies of a certain nationality it will be much faster to hire them.
~
Title: * 29
Instead of hiring Spies from Inns, you may train your own in Espionage Colleges. Please select your Espionage College, which is right next to your Inn.
~
Button : TRAIN
Title: * 30
Click on the 'Train C' icon to train Civilian Spies, the 'Train I' icon to train Infantry Spies and the 'Train S' icon to train Special Unit Spies.
~
Title: * 31
This last option will only be available if you have built the appropriate Special Structure.
~
Title: * 31
All of these Spies will be of the same nationality as the town from which they are recruited.
~
Title: * 31
You may set Rally Points for Espionage Colleges.
~
Title: * 31
This tutorial will proceed after you have sent your Civilian Spies into any of your Towns and Select the town.
~
Title: * 32
By sending Civilian Spies into your Towns, you will be helping to protect yourselves against enemy agents.
~
Title: * 32
Your Spies will work tirelessly, exposing and executing any enemy Spies who have been infiltrated into your Towns.
~
Title: * 32
One rule to remember is that you can only send in a Civilian Spy of the same nationality as your Town.
~
Title: * 33
Let's check out other abilities of your spies. Now Train and Mobilize an Infantry Spy from your Espionage College and Select it. 
~
Title: * 34
You cannot infiltrate a Spy into an enemy Town or Fort unless you change the color of his cloak to match the target Kingdom.
~
Title: * 34
To change the color, select the Spy and Click on the one of the colored balls.  If you see text stating, "Enemies Nearby!  Cannot Change Cloak!" it means just that.  
~
Title: * 34
You must wait until he is in the clear. 
~
Title: * 34
Change to gray if you want your Spy to pass for an Independent.
~
Title: * 34
Change back to your spy's original nation.
~
Title: * 35
One method of getting your Spies into enemy ranks is to make it look as if he has surrendered.
~
Button : SPYNOTI0
Title: * 35
Do this by selecting your Spy and, while he is still in your colors, Clicking on the Sneak Icon.  
~
Button : SPYNOTI0
Title: * 35
Sneaking is the default mode so you must change it if you wish to draw attention to your Spy.
~
Button : SPYNOTI1
Title: * 36
Clicking on the Icon will toggle it to the Surrender Icon.  Now when you change your Spy's color, the enemy will be notified of the "surrender".  
~
Button : SPYNOTI1
Title: * 36
They will then take control of your Spy and send him where they wish.
~
Button : NOSPY
Title: * 37
If you wish for your Spy to return to normal life, select him and then Click on the No Spy Icon.  
~
Button : NOSPY
Title: * 37
He will lay down his cloak and dagger and become a normal soldier or civilian.
~
Title: * 38
This tutorial will continue after you have sent your Civilian Spy into a foreign Town and selected the town. The target town's race must be the same as the spy's. 
~
Title: * 39
Once Spies have been infiltrated you should assign them a mission. 
~
Title: * 39
The default mission for Spies in foreign Towns or buildings is "Sleep".  A sleeping Spy will slowly build his spying skills.  
~
Title: * 39
It is unlikely that he will be exposed in this mode.
~
Button : SPY
Title: * 39
To change a Spy's mission, first Click on the Spy Menu Icon.  This icon shows that there is a Spy in this building or Town.
~
Button : CHG-TASK
Title: * 40
Spies infiltrated into enemy or Independent Towns may be used to "Agitate", which can lower an enemy Town's loyalty to its King and an Independent Town's resistance to your rule.
~
Button : CHG-TASK
Title: * 40
Begin Agitation by selecting the Town that your Spy has infiltrated and then Clicking on the Spy Menu Icon. 
~
Button : CHG-TASK
Title: * 40
Then select your Spy and Click on the Change Task Icon to change his job from Sleep to Agitation.
~
Title: * 41
You have successfully infiltrate your spy into a foreign town. Next, let's target a foreign Fort. 
~
Title: * 41
Unlike towns require same nationalities, you can send Infantry Spies into foreign Fort or Camp of any nationalities. 
~
Title: * 41
This tutorial will proceed after you have trained an Infantry Spy and sent it into a foreign Fort or Camp and selected the building. 
~
Title: * 42
The most useful Espionage task is Bribery which you do in Forts or Camps.  
~
Title: * 42
If you have a Spy in such a place, find him now and if you don't, infiltrate one.
~
Button : BRIBE
Title: * 43
To offer a bribe, select the infiltrated location, Click on your target (any enemy unit, except the King) and then Click on the Offer Bribe Icon.
~
Title: * 43
You will be asked how much money you are offering.  Click on the amount and then Click once again on the Offer Bribe Icon.  
~
Title: * 43
You will be told of your success or failure.
~
Title: * 43
If you have more than one Spy in the Fort you will be asked to choose the one who will offer the Bribe. 
~
Title: * 43
Select the foreign Fort or Camp with your spy inside.
~
Button : CAPTURE
Title: * 44
If you have a Spy who has become an enemy General or if you have successfully bribed an enemy General, 
~
Button : CAPTURE
Title: * 44
you will have the ability to capture the Fort or Camp that he commands.
~
Title: * 45
To do this, select the Fort or Camp and Click on the Capture Icon.  As soon as you do, the building will become yours.  
~
Title: * 45
This action is quite drastic, so you should expect that as soon as you capture the building the victim will declare war on you!
~
Title: * 45
If your Spy General is outside his Fort, changing his color back to your own will bring his entire Troop over to your side.
~
Title: * 46
It is important to remember that the success of your Spies will greatly depend upon their skill level.
~
Title: * 46
Spies with higher skill levels will have more missions that they will be able to attempt and they will be more likely to survive them.
~
Title: * 47
Select the foreign Fort or Camp with your spy inside.
~
Title: * 48
Click the Spy Menu Button.
~
Button : ASSASSIN
Title: * 49
If you wish to remove a pesky enemy General or King you should consider Assassination.
~
Button : ASSASSIN
Title: * 49
Assassinations may only take place in Forts or Camps.
~
Button : ASSASSIN
Title: * 49
To begin, select the Spy that you wish to use and then Click on the Assassinate Icon.  
~
Button : ASSASSIN
Title: * 49
You will only see this Icon if your spy has reached a skill level of 50 or more.
~
Button : ASSASSIN
Title: * 49
You will be informed on the likelihood of a successful attack and will be given the opportunity to cancel the mission.  
~
Button : ASSASSIN
Title: * 49
If you choose to go ahead, Click one more time on the Assassinate Icon.
~
Button : STEAL_T
Title: * 50
Stealing technology can be cheaper and faster than researching it yourself.
~
Button : STEAL_T
Title: * 50
To do this, select the Fort in which one of your Spies resides and Click on the Spy Menu Icon.  
~
Button : STEAL_T
Title: * 50
You will then see several Icons which denote tasks that your Spy can attempt.  Click on the Steal Technology Icon.
~
Button : STEAL_T
Title: * 50
You will be shown your chances of completing the mission successfully.  If you choose to go ahead, Click on Yes.
~
Button : VSECRET
Title: * 51
Just as you can view information on your own Kingdom, by clicking on the Kingdoms, Towns, Economy, Trade, Military, Tech and Rank buttons
~
Button : VSECRET
Title: * 51
So you can view the same information of other Kingdoms if you have infiltrated a Spy into their midst.
~
Button : VSECRET
Title: * 51
To do this, select the location of your Spy, Click on the Spy Eye Icon and then on the View Information Icon.  
~
Button : VSECRET
Title: * 51
When you do you will see a list of the subjects that a Spy of that skill level can view.
~
Button : VSECRET
Title: * 51
Spies with higher skill levels will be able to view more sensitive information.
~
Button : INCIDENT
Title: * 52
Spies in enemy Forts will be able to manufacture an incident that will cause diplomatic problems or even war between one Kingdom (where he is infiltrated) and another Kingdom.  
~
Button : INCIDENT
Title: * 52
This can be extremely useful if you wish to start a war between two strong opponents.
~
Button : INCIDENT
Title: * 52
To create an incident you will need to have a Spy with a skill level of at least 90.
~
Button : INCIDENT
Title: * 52
Select your Spy and Click on the Create Incident Icon.  You must then choose a target Kingdom.  You will be informed of the chances of success.  
~
Button : INCIDENT
Title: * 52
If you choose to proceed, Click once again on the Create Incident Icon.
~
Button : MOBILSPY
Title: * 53
You may sometimes wish to extract a Spy from an enemy Town, Fort or Camp.  
~
Button : MOBILSPY
Title: * 53
To do this, select the Spy's hiding place and then select the Spy.
~
Button : MOBILSPY
Title: * 53
When you Click on the Mobilize Spy Icon, your Spy will leave the building or Town and stand outside.  
~
Button : MOBILSPY
Title: * 53
You may then send him elsewhere but it would be wise to change his cloak color before you do so.  
~
Button : MOBILSPY
Title: * 53
If you don't you risk his exposure and execution.
~
Title: * 54
To finish this tutorial. You have to achieve 500 Population and 200 Military Score.
~
Title: * 54
You always can check the game goals and your scores by pressing the F8 key or by clicking on the 'Rank' button at the top of the screen.	
~